{"id": "EUVD-2016-10915", "enisaUuid": "53142212-d73d-3682-b7e1-38ab631cb80b", "description": "L-SMASH through 2.14.5 contains an infinite loop vulnerability in vc1_importer_probe() in importer/vc1_imp.c that allows attackers to hang applications via crafted input files. Attackers can supply a file consisting only of zero bytes, which lsmash_read_file() probes automatically, causing indefinite CPU consumption and denial of service.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T14:16:26", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T17:44:42", "baseScore": 6.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/l-smash/l-smash/pull/58", "https://github.com/l-smash/l-smash/blob/v2.14.5/importer/vc1_imp.c#L462-L488", "https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/l-smash-hevc-importer-double-free", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/l-smash-through-2.14.5-infinite-loop-in-vc-1-importer-probe"], "aliases": ["CVE-2016-20099", "GHSA-wq77-gg6m-97hh"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.24, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "52738175-2ad4-3533-9a4f-b4019dd6b5d5", "product": {"name": "l-smash", "vendor": {"name": "l-smash"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22642.14.5"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "1453be27-c731-3da6-9c1e-fe1d202bc60d", "vendor": {"name": "l-smash"}}], "isExploited": false}